# Inherits the repository's checks and turns off exactly one.
#
# clang-analyzer-security.ArrayBound reports "Out of bound access to memory
# preceding the region" inside LLVM's own `User::getHungOffOperands`, which is
# `*(reinterpret_cast<Use **>(this) - 1)` — a deliberate, documented part of
# LLVM's hung-off-operand layout, and the analyzer has no way to know the
# allocation extends backwards. Every `IRBuilder` call that builds a PHI or a
# comparison walks through it, so the report reappears on whichever file in
# this module happens to be analysed first, and the diagnostic itself lands in
# an LLVM header where no NOLINT can be written.
#
# Scoped to this module, which is the only one that includes LLVM headers, so
# the check keeps running over every line of Volt's own code.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -clang-analyzer-security.ArrayBound
